Add:

```js
function setControlHint() {
  ui.controlHint.innerHTML = onFoot
    ? '<span><b>WASD</b> WALK</span><span><b>SHIFT</b> SPRINT</span><span><b>SPACE</b> JUMP</span><span><b>F</b> ENTER CAR</span><span><b>ESC</b> PAUSE</span>'
    : ...
}
```

But innerHTML on every toggle fine.

```js
function updateFootUi() {
  ui.hud.classList.toggle('on-foot', onFoot);
  ui.useBtn.querySelector('span').textContent = onFoot ? 'ENTER' : 'EXIT';
  ui.useBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', onFoot ? 'Enter car' : 'Exit car');
  ui.speedMode.textContent = onFoot ? 'ON FOOT' : 'SUPERSONIC';
  ui.enterPrompt.classList.toggle('is-hidden', !onFoot); // but only when near? handle in updateHud
  ...
}
```
We want the enter prompt only when near. In updateHud (called every ~0.06s), when onFoot:
```
const dist = Math.hypot(character.pos.x-player.pos.x, character.pos.z-player.pos.z);
const near = dist < 8;
ui.enterPrompt.classList.toggle('is-hidden', !(onFoot && near));
```
When not on foot hide. `enterPrompt` text says F ENTER CAR; fine.

Control hint is hidden on mobile via CSS anyway.

Foot functions: exit/enter. We'll add after resetPlayerCar maybe.

```js
function exitCar() {
  if (onFoot || mode !== 'playing' || paused) return;
  if (!player.grounded || player.speed > 10) { showBanner('SLOW DOWN', 'TO STEP OUT', '', 1.1); return; }
  onFoot = true;
  character.spawn(player.pos, player.yaw);
  character.root.visible = true;
  footYaw = player.yaw;
  footPitch = 0.18;
  footLookIdle = 0;
  footKickCooldown = 0;
  cameraMode = 'foot';
  setControlHint(true);
  updateFootUi();
  hintTimer = 7;
  ui.controlHint.style.opacity = '1';
  showBanner('ON FOOT', 'F TO ENTER CAR', '', 1.4);
  sound.ui();
}

function enterCar(silent = false) {
  if (!onFoot) return;
  if (!silent) {
    const d = Math.hypot(character.pos.x - player.pos.x, character.pos.z - player.pos.z);
    if (d > 8) {
      showBanner('TOO FAR', 'WALK BACK TO YOUR CAR', '', 1.1);
      return;
    }
  }
  onFoot = false;
  character.hide();
  cameraMode = 'chase';
  setControlHint(false);
  updateFootUi();
  ui.enterPrompt.classList.add('is-hidden');
  if (!silent) {
    showBanner('BACK IN THE DRIVER SEAT', '', '', 0.9);
    sound.ui();
  }
}
```

`updateFootUi()` toggles hud class, speedMode, use label, hint.

For force entering at kickoff, call `enterCar(true)` before resetting positions and camera. But onFoot and character depends. Add in resetKickoff at start:
```
if (onFoot) enterCar(true);
```
enterCar sets cameraMode chase; then resetKickoff sets it anyway.

Similarly startMatch calls resetKickoff so fine. quitToMenu: `if (onFoot) enterCar(true);`. Also hide character.

setHudVisible(false) at boot hides touch controls.

Now collideCharacterBall:

```js
function collideCharacterBall() {
  const cx = character.pos.x;
  const cy = character.pos.y + 1.2;
  const cz = character.pos.z;
  const R = ball.radius + 0.9;
  const dx = ball.pos.x - cx, dy = ball.pos.y - cy, dz = ball.pos.z - cz;
  const dist = Math.hypot(dx,dy,dz);
  if (dist >= R || dist < 0.0001) return;
  const nx = dx/dist, ny = dy/dist, nz = dz/dist;
  const pen = R - dist + 0.01;
  ball.pos.x += nx*pen; ball.pos.y += ny*pen; ball.pos.z += nz*pen;
  if (footKickCooldown > 0) return;
  footKickCooldown = 0.35;
  const charSpeed = Math.hypot(character.vel.x, character.vel.z);
  const power = 10 + charSpeed*1.25;
  ball.vel.multiplyScalar(0.35);
  ball.vel.x += nx*power;
  ball.vel.z += nz*power;
  ball.vel.y += Math.max(0, ny)*power*0.35 + 2.5;
  if (ball.vel.length() > 70) ball.vel.setLength(70);
  ball.pos.y = Math.max(ball.pos.y, ball.radius);
  ball.lastHitBy = 'blue';
  ball.lastHitTime = simTime;
  sound.hit(power/30);
  shake = Math.max(shake, 0.12);
  effects.emit(ball.pos, {...});
}
```

Note normal points from character to ball, so pushing along normal moves ball away. Good. If the character stands on top? fine.

Ball may hit character from behind and get pushed; okay.

Also character collision with the car? If the player walks into the parked car, they could walk through. Add simple separation: push character out of car's OBB approximated by ellipse. Optional. Let's add a simple circle-car collision in character update? Character doesn't know car. Could do in main:
```js
function collideCharacterCar() {
  const dx = character.pos.x - player.pos.x, dz = ...;
  const localX = dx*cos - dz*sin? car local; if within car extents + 0.6, push out.
}
```
Not necessary for functionality; but walking through your own car looks bad. Add a simple circular repulsion radius 3.0:
```
const d = hypot(dx,dz);
if (d < 3.1) push character out to 3.1.
```
The car is 5 long, 2.55 wide, so a 3.1 circle is a rough approximation. Good enough.

Bot car collision with character? Could push character if the bot drives into them. Add same for botCar radius 3.0; push character away. Optional but fun. In `collideCharacterCar` loop over cars:
```
for (const car of [player, botCar]) { ... }
```
The car doesn't get pushed (character is light), but maybe the car slows slightly. Fine.

Camera update:
In `updateCamera(dt)`, after the goal branch and before chase:
```js
if (onFoot) { updateFootCamera(dt); return; }
```
Note `cameraMode === 'goal'` takes precedence: when a goal happens while on foot, the goal cam shows, then kickoff enters car. Fine.

`updateFootCamera(dt)`:
```js
function updateFootCamera(dt) {
  const forward = tmpA.set(Math.cos(footYaw), 0, -Math.sin(footYaw));
  const dist = 9.5 + footPitch * 4;
  const height = 3.6 + footPitch * 8.5;
  camDesired.set(character.pos.x - forward.x*dist, character.pos.y + height, character.pos.z - forward.z*dist);
  camDesired.x = clamp(camDesired.x, -FIELD.halfLength + 1.5, FIELD.halfLength - 1.5);
  camDesired.z = clamp(camDesired.z, -FIELD.halfWidth + 1.5, FIELD.halfWidth - 1.5);
  camDesired.y = clamp(camDesired.y, 1.8, 24);
  camera.position.lerp(camDesired, 1 - Math.exp(-6.5*dt));
  camLook.copy(character.pos).add(tmpB.set(0, 2.35, 0)).addScaledVector(forward, 2.5);
  camera.lookAt(camLook);
  camera.fov = damp(camera.fov, 66, 4, dt);
  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
  applyShake(dt);
}
```
But tmpA/tmpB are used elsewhere inside this function and applyShake; fine.

Better camera collision: if camera desired is behind the goal wall? Clamp to arena interior; when near the goal end, camera clamps to x=±48.5, might be inside the goal. Fine.

Foot look handling:
```js
function applyFootLook(lookX, lookY, dt) {
  if (!onFoot) return;
  if (lookX || lookY) {
    footYaw = wrapAngle(footYaw + lookX * 0.0052);
    footPitch = clamp(footPitch + lookY * 0.0038, -0.12, 0.72);
    footLookIdle = 0;
  } else {
    footLookIdle += dt;
  }
  if (footLookIdle > 1.4 && character.speed > 2.5) {
    footYaw = wrapAngle(footYaw + wrapAngle(character.yaw - footYaw) * Math.min(1, 1.4 * dt));
  }
}
```
Careful sign of footPitch: positive = camera higher looking down. Drag down (lookY positive) -> camera higher / look down. Fine.

`wrapAngle` not imported in main.js currently: import from constants. Add.

Update `updatePlaying`:

Current:
```
const controls = input.sample();
if (controls.reset) resetPlayerCar();
player.update(dt, controls, effects);
const botControls = bot.update(dt, { ball, botCar, time: simTime });
botCar.update(dt, botControls, effects);
...
collideCarBall(player);
collideCarBall(botCar);
collideCars();
